<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent incidents continue across South Sudan, including a grenade explosion in Northern Bahr el Ghazal that killed four children and injured two, and the killing of an Ugandan driver in Juba that prompted transporters to demand compensation and the government to be urged to pay the victim's family. The government sent 25 young professionals to Brazil for specialized farming training and President Salva Kiir traveled to Ethiopia, while UNHCR and South Sudan officials held talks to improve support for refugees in Egypt. The UCDP recorded two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxNZ1BSWHJMaG1uRFFnYU5TUUIwMS14bzlFVkxuR21razB5d2Ytc3pkckhNWWNXQjI5OW15OTkwZnFVd0tULXdCS3RIVTNiX1doSTZTNVRTMWFwYkdNWHp2dXhURUFWTTJGNUNlR3NNb2hrUXE5b1puWjV6MnVQdnp0d2V3akhWdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxPcmZKNFUybE14RGh6TGlBS29IaUUtLXVCZDUxZ0tvSmVEWnpvcXY0bm90R19QdGxqQm9JeU1IeVRPX2R4blVZUG5ubDFnNmFUYVhfLWRjWXhMdkptejk4MXVyNVZ4VC0zazVvRFR2MVFjclMyYU01eW4ta3ZHWGxuRGdKRFdrOV9MTDFFMnFNd1NhYkF4SVp3YVJB?oc=5&quot;&gt;Yeni Şafak English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxQQzB1WnJNdkxtSndrb2xUQ0ozdVFNRllpTGljdk9ncEYyOEFVdkZ3UW1YaVVqUmkyRFVuZEtiR1BIOXUtUjJqaGlsWTNyUnc5M3FBUFVKd3ZQaUtqQ2dGeDhHTllKUUNPb0g4dHFkWGc2TldUQjExRW8yUnlib0VfQ2JHcGhfeXptVEdJUkFfdWUyTUswWFRDdVJOVmRPdlA4QXhjQ2pvYw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Monitor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Arabiya English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Monitor&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxPMTVDcnRhUl9CT0FBMUdDU2xBM2d